[1m[38;5;231mWhere should the userId be stored, and for how long?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mlocalStorage (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSurvives browser restart, cleared on explicit logout. Available to every form from day one. Script-readable, [39m
     [38;5;246macceptable for a non-credential identifier.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m sessionStorage
     [38;5;246mCleared when the tab closes. Safer on shared machines, but returning users are unidentified and each tab is [39m
     [38;5;246mindependent.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Cookie
     [38;5;246mSent to the server automatically. Right choice if the server needs it — but the secure HttpOnly form can't be read
[39m     [38;5;246mby JS, so callers couldn't pass it.[39m
